WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:06.130
Dr. Kowalski prepared three copies of the
February 9, 2016 edition of the New York Times

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.210
for testing.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.790
A copy was placed on the setting 1:1, and
the output produced was one copy of the February

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:16.219
9, 2016 edition of the Cleveland, Ohio Plain
Dealer.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:19.109
Another copy was placed on the setting "Very
Fine."

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:23.990
The output produced was a copy of the February
10, 2016 edition of The New York Times.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:29.310
An examination of the paper revealed large
blank sections, and the final four pages were

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.710
completely blank.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.629
The text consistently changed while being
observed, prompting researchers to hypothesize

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:40.039
that they were seeing the draft of the issue
appear as it was being written.

